# Used as a fallback businessName on new estimates if a business record can't be read.
DEFAULT_BUSINESS_NAME="Your Business"

# Protects /api/follow-ups/generate (the daily cron endpoint) from being
# triggered by anyone who finds the URL. Requests must send
# `Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>` — Vercel does this automatically for
# its own Cron Jobs once this is set as a project environment variable.
# REQUIRED in production: the endpoint returns 500 if it's unset there (fail
# closed), since it triggers Gmail scans and reply syncs. Optional in dev.
# Generate with `openssl rand -hex 32`.
CRON_SECRET=

# Optional but recommended in production: Upstash Redis backs the login/signup/
# intake rate limiters (lib/rateLimit.ts). Without these, the limiter falls
# back to per-instance in-memory counters — fine for dev, but NOT shared across
# serverless instances, so the limits aren't a hard guarantee. Create a free
# database at https://console.upstash.com/redis and copy its REST URL + token.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# Signs/verifies session JWTs (lib/auth.ts) — this is NOT a password, and
# rotating it logs out every business at once. Generate a random one with
# `openssl rand -hex 32` and never reuse it across projects. Each business
# has its own email + password, stored (hashed) in the Businesses table —
# see the "Accounts" section in README.md.
AUTH_SECRET=

# One Google Cloud OAuth client shared by every tenant's self-serve Gmail +
# Calendar consent flow (not a per-tenant credential — each business gets its
# own refresh token via /api/oauth/google/start, encrypted at rest). Create a
# "Web application" OAuth client at
# https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials with authorized redirect
# URIs `http://localhost:3000/api/oauth/google/callback` (dev) and
# `https://<your-domain>/api/oauth/google/callback` (prod), and add
# gmail.send, gmail.readonly, and calendar.events scopes on the OAuth consent
# screen. See "Google connection" in README.md.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Second mailbox provider — Microsoft identity platform (v2.0/Entra) OAuth
# client, alongside Google above (services/microsoftOAuth.ts,
# services/providers/microsoftMailboxProvider.ts). Optional: unlike Google,
# Microsoft isn't required for the app to run — /api/oauth/microsoft/start
# returns a clear error if these aren't set. Register an app at
# https://entra.microsoft.com (App registrations > New registration),
# "Accounts in any organizational directory and personal Microsoft
# accounts" (multi-tenant, matches MICROSOFT_TENANT=common below), platform
# "Web", redirect URI `http://localhost:3000/api/oauth/microsoft/callback`
# (dev) and `https://<your-domain>/api/oauth/microsoft/callback` (prod).
# Under Certificates & secrets, create a client secret (this is
# MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET — copy the secret VALUE, not its ID). Under API
# permissions, add Microsoft Graph delegated scopes Mail.Send and
# Mail.ReadWrite (openid/email/offline_access are requested automatically,
# no manifest change needed).
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=

# "common" (the default if unset) accepts both personal Microsoft accounts
# and work/school (Azure AD) accounts through the same app registration —
# see config/microsoft.ts. Only change this if you specifically want to
# restrict connections to one Azure AD tenant.
MICROSOFT_TENANT=common

# Optional explicit override for the OAuth redirect_uri. If unset, the
# Microsoft OAuth routes derive it from the incoming request's own host
# (same as Google's flow) — set this only if your Azure AD app registration
# needs an exact, single registered redirect URI. Must exactly match a URI
# registered on the app above, including the http(s) scheme.
MICROSOFT_REDIRECT_URI=

# Encrypts each business's mailbox refresh token — Google's and, if
# connected, Microsoft's (lib/crypto.ts, AES-256-GCM) — before writing it to
# the database, which has no field-level encryption of its own. Generate
# with `openssl rand -hex 32`. Losing/rotating this key without a
# re-encryption migration means every business must reconnect every provider.
TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# Supabase — the database (Postgres). Required; every read/write in the app
# goes through it (see lib/supabase.ts, services/db.ts, services/business.ts).
# Project URL and keys are under Project Settings > API in the Supabase
# dashboard. NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is the "publishable" key (safe to
# expose client-side, though nothing here currently does); SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
# is the "secret" key (server only — bypasses Row Level Security, never
# expose it client-side). Schema lives in supabase/migrations/*.sql, applied
# via the linked Supabase CLI (`supabase db push`) — see CLAUDE.md.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Gmail push notifications — real-time reply sync (services/gmailWatch.ts,
# services/gmailWatchSync.ts), on top of the daily cron/manual "Check for new
# replies" sync. Optional: leave both unset and the app behaves exactly as
# before (push registration silently no-ops). To enable:
#   1. In Google Cloud Console, create a Pub/Sub topic and grant Publish
#      permission on it to gmail-api-push@system.gserviceaccount.com.
#   2. Create a push subscription on that topic with endpoint
#      `https://<your-domain>/api/webhooks/gmail-push?token=<GMAIL_PUSH_SECRET>`
#      (the token below, appended as a query param since Pub/Sub push has no
#      per-request HMAC of its own — see that route's doc comment).
#   3. Set GMAIL_PUBSUB_TOPIC to the full topic name,
#      e.g. `projects/<project-id>/topics/gmail-replies`.
GMAIL_PUBSUB_TOPIC=
GMAIL_PUSH_SECRET=

# Admin provisioning (/admin) — lets the agency create/activate a client
# workspace in one action instead of editing the database directly (see
# CLAUDE.md's "Access & entitlement" section). Set this to the `id` (uuid)
# of your OWN workspace (sign up like any client, then copy its id from the
# `workspaces` table) — only that workspace's owner session can reach /admin.
# Optional: leave unset and /admin is unreachable by anyone.
ADMIN_WORKSPACE_ID=

# Inbound-email lead classifier (services/leadClassification.ts) — calls
# Claude Haiku via the Anthropic API to decide whether a newly-scanned Gmail
# thread is a genuine new-work lead, and logs the decision to
# lead_classifications (migration 0016) for review at /admin/classifications.
# Classify-and-log only: no sending, drafting, or follow-ups depend on this.
# Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys. Optional: leave
# unset and classification is skipped (logged, not thrown) — the daily cron's
# other jobs (follow-ups, reply sync, Gmail lead capture) are unaffected.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
